This product includes software developed by Paul Miller.

  @noble/hashes 2.4.0
  Copyright (c) 2022 Paul Miller (https://paulmillr.com)
  Licensed under the MIT License. See node_modules/@noble/hashes/LICENSE
  for the full text, which is reproduced below.

  Used for: SHA-256, SHA-512, RIPEMD-160, HMAC and PBKDF2.

  Why a dependency at all, when the rest of this repository has none:
  these must be SYNCHRONOUS. The browser provides hashing only through
  crypto.subtle, which is asynchronous, and the application calls them
  synchronously in 34 places. Node's crypto cannot be bundled for a
  browser at all. ⇒ A pure-JS implementation is required, and a widely
  used, actively maintained, independently reviewed one is more likely
  to be correct than a fresh implementation of the same specifications.

