Third-party data
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  impl/js/data/wordlist-english.mjs
  BIP-39's official English wordlist, from bitcoin/bips.
  BIP-39 is public specification text.

  Reproduced because the standard requires exactly these words in
  exactly this order: substituting any of them produces a wallet no
  other implementation can restore. It is data, not code.

  ⚠ It is a MODULE rather than the original text file because the
  wallet is browser-only and there is no filesystem to read from. The
  words are unchanged. test/bip39.mjs reconstructs the file's exact
  form and checks its sha256 against the published one:
    2f5eed53a4727b4bf8880d8f3f199efc90e58503646d9ff8eff3a2ed3b24dbda
  ⇒ so "byte-identical to the official list" is a checked claim rather
  than an assertion in a document.

